    reload: one index attempt per game list update (#300)
    
    reloadAllGames started the achievements index twice: SystemData::loadConfig
    runs the startup index whenever it is handed a window (fork #183), and the
    start added under UPDATE GAMELISTS for D-RA-035 (fork #299), guarded only
    by isRunning(), fired exactly when that one had failed -- offline -- and
    fetched the hash library again at once. On guest d (48f940aa06, proof-298
    phase E): the first attempt ended at its stall bound 35 s after the reload
    with the toast and the marker, the second began the moment it failed and
    succeeded when the link came back twelve seconds later, so the interface
    sat on LOADING for a minute and the link's return carried an index nobody
    asked for; on a device offline it would be twice the wait and two toasts.
    
    The second start is dropped; the comment says why. One attempt per reload,
    loadConfig's. tools/es-syntax-check PASS.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

